# Run r1102b, slice 2, boot N: three removals in one fresh normal world (prep_srv.sh OUT_N s2n B), then boot:
#   - fruitsdelight-0.5.11.jar out of srv/mods (SQ-FR-05; no mod in mods/ declares a dependency on it)
#   - FarmersRespite-1.19-2.0.jar out of srv/mods (SQ-CDQ-03; no dependents either)
#   - srv/kubejs/data/creativedelight/ deleted (SQ-WCD-06: rules, scripts and features from the CD jar copy)
# The wild-crop counts then drop by the Fruits Delight and Respite rows (each named in a "mod not loaded, skipped" line).
# Probes: zz_zq_probe.js, zz_count.js.
pace 2

## SQ-FR-05 | Creative Delight loads without Fruits Delight
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject (?i)mixin apply failed|InvalidInjectionException
bootreject ClassNotFoundException.*dev\.xkmc\.fruitsdelight|NoClassDefFoundError.*dev/xkmc/fruitsdelight
bootreject Error occurred while handling event.*fruitsdelight/
kjsreject (?i)error.*fruitsdelight/
shell ls mods | grep -ci fruitsdelight; ! ls mods | grep -qi fruitsdelight
shell grep -iE "fruitsdelight" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/kubejs/startup.log | head -8; true
look the kubejs lines show the Fruits Delight scripts skipped by their "// requires: fruitsdelight" header (or no line at all), no error

## SQ-CDQ-03 | Creative Delight loads without Farmer's Respite; pot buffer still works
bootreject (?i)farmersrespite.*creativedelight\.mixins\.json|creativedelight\.mixins\.json.*farmersrespite
bootreject /(ERROR|FATAL)\].*ClassNotFoundException.*umpaz\.farmersrespite
shell ! ls mods | grep -qi farmersrespite
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s2nhome] run summon minecraft:marker ~ 201 ~ {Tags:["s2nhome"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s2nhome,limit=1] Pos
capture N entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> forceload add {N1-8} {N3-8} {N1+24} {N3+24}
sleep 5
> fill {N1-2} {N2-1} {N3-2} {N1+20} {N2-1} {N3+20} minecraft:stone
> fill {N1-2} {N2} {N3-2} {N1+20} {N2+4} {N3+20} minecraft:air
> setblock {N1+2} {N2} {N3+2} minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item]
> setblock {N1+2} {N2+1} {N3+2} farmersdelight:cooking_pot{Inventory:{Size:9,Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:glow_berries",Count:1b},{Slot:1b,id:"farmersdelight:milk_bottle",Count:1b},{Slot:2b,id:"minecraft:egg",Count:1b},{Slot:3b,id:"minecraft:sugar",Count:1b}]}}
sleep 25
> data get block {N1+2} {N2+1} {N3+2}
> zcount {N1-1} {N2-1} {N3-1} {N1+5} {N2+3} {N3+5}
waitlog \[zcount\] entities 30
expect farmersdelight:glow_berry_custard
expect minecraft:glass_bottle
reject item:minecraft:glass_bottle

## SQ-WCD-06 | wild crop rules and features from the CD jar (pack folder copy deleted)
shell test ! -d kubejs/data/creativedelight
bootexpect \[wild-crops\] \d+ crop modifiers added, \d+ mod modifiers off, \d+ biome-file patches removed
bootexpect \[wild-crops\] \d+ crop/biome pairs in \d+ crop tags
bootreject \[wild-crops\] could not read
bootreject \[wild-crops\] .*(no such biome|is not in #creativedelight:wild_crops/)
bootexpect \[creativedelight\] server scripts ready
shell grep -E "\[wild-crops\]" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-300
> execute positioned {N1+10} {N2} {N3+10} run place feature creativedelight:wild/cabbages ~ ~ ~
reject Unknown|ERROR
look counts as SQ-WCD-01 minus the fruitsdelight and farmersrespite rows (named in "mod not loaded, skipped" lines); /place feature only proves the jar's configured feature loads (on stone it may place nothing: "Failed to place feature" is fine)
